# Redgres core

Before work, read `AGENTS.md` and `CONTEXT.md`; inspect Git and preserve dirty/user work. Read `docs/PROJECT_CHARTER.md` for product scope/acceptance decisions and `docs/INDEX.md` only when `AGENTS.md` does not route the task. Derive implementation truth from code, tests, Git, and the relevant `docs/TRACEABILITY.md` row—not target prose or chat memory.

Load only routed headings/endpoints from `AGENTS.md`. Identify governing PRD IDs, acceptance criteria, invariants, and ADRs before editing. Implementation/review work also reads `.cursor/rules/05-evidence-first-engineering.mdc`; autonomous coding reads `.cursor/rules/06-continuous-orchestration.mdc`.

The sibling repositories `../database-app` and `../redis-ui` are read-only references. Redgres code and artifacts stay in this repository. Never copy secrets/runtime files, push, or change production, DNS, Cloudflare, credentials, or legacy services without separate explicit authorization.

Behavior changes update their canonical owner and `docs/TRACEABILITY.md`. Run focused checks while developing and the required complete gates before handoff.
